{"id":"torrey:ostrich-the","source":"torrey","name":"Ostrich, The","slug":"ostrich-the","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Unclean and unfit for food — Le 11:13.","refs":[["Lev",11,13,11,13]]},{"text":"Furnished with wings and feathers — Job 39:13.","refs":[["Job",39,13,39,13]]},{"text":"Lays her eggs in the sand — Job 39:14.","refs":[["Job",39,14,39,14]]},{"text":"Void of wisdom. — Job 39:17.","refs":[["Job",39,17,39,17]]},{"text":"Imprudent. — Job 39:15.","refs":[["Job",39,15,39,15]]},{"text":"Cruel to her young. — Job 39:16.","refs":[["Job",39,16,39,16]]},{"text":"Rapid in movement. — Job 39:18.","refs":[["Job",39,18,39,18]]},{"text":"Of the unnatural cruelty of the Jews in their calamities. — La 4:3.","refs":[["Lam",4,3,4,3]]},{"text":"(Companionship with,) of extreme desolation. — Job 30:29.","refs":[["Job",30,29,30,29]]}],"refCount":9}
